WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.663
Who authorizes all this?

2
00:00:01.663 --> 00:00:08.985
AWS's services-in-scope page, updated October
fifteenth, 2026, lists one row, Amazon

3
00:00:08.985 --> 00:00:15.651
Route 53, in scope for FedRAMP Class C,
formerly Moderate, in US East and West.

4
00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:18.693
There are no separate rows
for the Resolver features;

5
00:00:18.693 --> 00:00:22.150
generally available features
are in scope unless excluded.

6
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.237
For a Moderate civilian workload
in the commercial Regions,

7
00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:30.650
where the program's AWS workloads
run, that covers the DNS service.

8
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.975
As an inference, note that
in the system security plan.

9
00:00:33.975 --> 00:00:39.000
Microsoft's audit-scope page has one DNS
row, in scope for FedRAMP High in Azure

10
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.090
commercial, with no separate row for
the Private Resolver or resolver policy.
